---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '@/components/Header.astro';
import { withBase } from '@/lib/paths';

/*
 * The privacy policy.
 *
 * Every factual claim here was checked against the product before it was
 * written — what the patient app actually sends, what it is shown back, how a
 * phone is identified, what is logged, where it is hosted. A privacy policy is
 * enforceable in a way a marketing page is not, so nothing in it is aspiration
 * and nothing is boilerplate borrowed from another company's site.
 *
 * It covers the United States service only, and says so in its first lines.
 * The Chennai deployment is a different product in privacy terms — an
 * on-premises machine with no internet, no cloud, and DPDP rather than HIPAA —
 * and it needs its own page rather than a paragraph bolted onto this one.
 * Write that before the first Indian patient, not before the first login.
 *
 * `LAST_UPDATED` is shown to the reader and is the date the *wording* last
 * changed, not the date of the last deploy. Change it when the text changes,
 * and say what changed in the section that promises exactly that.
 */
const LAST_UPDATED = '19 September 2026';

// Named here rather than inline so the two places it appears cannot drift.
const SUPPORT_EMAIL = 'support@refresh.health';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Refresh Health"
  description="What Refresh Health does with information about you: what the patient app sends, what is stored, where it is held, how long it is kept, and how to ask for it."
  pageStylesheet={withBase('/assets/css/privacy.css')}
>

<section class="legal-hero">
  <Header />
  <div class="container legal-hero__inner">
    <h1 class="legal-hero__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-hero__meta">Refresh Health, Inc. &middot; Last updated {LAST_UPDATED}</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="legal">
  <div class="container legal__doc">

    <p class="body">This policy explains what Refresh Health does with information about you.
      It is written to be read, not to be got past. If anything here is unclear,
      the contact details at the end are real and answered.</p>

    <p class="body">It covers the Refresh Health service as offered in the <strong>United States</strong>.</p>

    <h2>Two different things, governed differently</h2>

    <p>It matters which of these you are using, because the rules are not the same.</p>

    <table class="legal__table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th></th><th>What it is</th><th>Who is responsible</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>This website</strong></td>
          <td>Our public pages, and the form you can use to contact us.</td>
          <td>Refresh Health. This policy governs it.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>The clinical platform and the patient app</strong></td>
          <td>Your medical record, your measurements, and the app your practice connects to your chart.</td>
          <td>Your healthcare practice. We hold that information for them and act only on their instructions.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <p>In short: information you give <em>this website</em> is ours to look after.
      Information in <em>your medical record</em> belongs to the practice treating you.</p>

    <h2>Who is responsible for your medical information</h2>

    <p>Your healthcare practice decides what is recorded about you, why, and who
      may see it. Under United States health privacy law that makes the practice
      the <em>covered entity</em> &mdash; the party responsible for your record
      &mdash; and Refresh Health its <em>business associate</em>, acting only on
      its instructions and under a written agreement.</p>

    <p>Refresh Health provides the software the practice uses. We process your
      information only on their instructions and for no purpose of our own. We do
      not sell it, rent it, or use it for advertising. We do not use it to train
      anything for anybody else. Each practice&rsquo;s information is kept
      separate from every other practice&rsquo;s.</p>

    <h2>If you contact us through this website</h2>

    <p>The contact form collects what you type into it &mdash; your name, your
      email address, and whatever you tell us &mdash; and we use it to answer you
      and for nothing else.</p>

    <p>The form is delivered to us by <strong>Formspree</strong>, which passes
      the message on and does not use it for anything of its own.</p>

    <p><strong>Please do not send medical details through it.</strong> It is an
      ordinary enquiry form, not a way into your record. If you have a question
      about your care, speak to your practice.</p>

    <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>

    <p>This website sets <strong>one cookie</strong>, which keeps your session
      working while you are on the site and is discarded afterwards. There is no
      analytics, no advertising pixel, and no tracking of you across other
      websites. Nothing on this site reports your visit to another company.</p>

    <h2>What the patient app sends us</h2>

    <p>When you record a measurement in the app &mdash; a blood pressure, a
      weight, a blood glucose, an oxygen level or a heart rate &mdash; the app sends:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>the kind of measurement, and its number or numbers</li>
      <li>the unit it was measured in</li>
      <li>the date and time you took it</li>
    </ul>

    <p>That is all of it. The app does not attach your name, your date of birth
      or anything else to a measurement: whose reading it is comes from your
      sign-in, not from the message itself.</p>

    <h2>Apple Health and Health Connect</h2>

    <p><strong>The app reads health measurements from Apple Health (on iPhone)
      and Health Connect (on Android)</strong>, so that readings you have already
      taken &mdash; on a blood pressure cuff, a scale, an oximeter or a glucose
      meter that writes to your phone &mdash; can reach your practice without you
      typing them in again.</p>

    <p>It reads the kinds of measurement this service is for: blood pressure,
      weight, blood glucose, oxygen saturation and heart rate. It does not read
      your whole health record, and it does not write to it.</p>

    <p>This happens only after you have given permission on the phone itself, and
      you can withdraw that permission at any time in your phone&rsquo;s settings
      &mdash; in Settings &rarr; Health &rarr; Data Access &amp; Devices on
      iPhone, or in Health Connect on Android. Withdrawing it stops the app
      reading anything further; measurements already sent to your practice remain
      part of your medical record.</p>

    <p>Health information read from your phone is used only to place it in your
      medical record for your practice. <strong>It is never used for advertising,
      marketing, or any form of data mining</strong>, by us or by anybody else.</p>

    <h2>Other companies whose software is inside the app</h2>

    <p>The app uses <strong>AWS AppSync</strong>, a service of Amazon Web
      Services, to communicate with our servers. Amazon processes that traffic on
      our behalf under contract and does not use it for its own purposes.</p>

    <p>There is no advertising software in the app, and nothing in it profiles you.</p>

    <h2>What the app shows you</h2>

    <p>The app receives the name of your practice and your own initials. It is
      not sent your full name, your date of birth or your address.</p>

    <h2>How your phone is recognised</h2>

    <p>When your practice connects your phone, the app creates a key inside the
      phone&rsquo;s own secure hardware. That key never leaves the phone and
      cannot be copied off it. Your phone is also given a random identifier so
      the service can tell one connected phone from another.</p>

    <p>Signing in produces a pass that lasts fifteen minutes and is then renewed.
      If your phone is lost or stolen, your practice can disconnect it, and it
      stops working on its very next request.</p>

    <h2>What we record for safety</h2>

    <p>Because this is a medical record, we must be able to answer &ldquo;who
      looked at this?&rdquo;. We therefore keep a record of every attempt to sign
      in &mdash; successful or not &mdash; and of your chart being connected to a
      phone and each time that phone reads your record afterwards.</p>

    <p>These records exist to protect you. They are never used to build a profile
      of you, and never for marketing.</p>

    <h2>Where your information is kept</h2>

    <p>Your information is held on servers we operate at <strong>Amazon Web
      Services in Northern Virginia, United States</strong>. It stays in the
      United States.</p>

    <p>Amazon acts as our sub-processor under a written agreement: it stores and
      moves the information and makes no use of it. Information is encrypted
      while it travels and while it is stored.</p>

    <h2>Who your information is shared with</h2>

    <table class="legal__table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Who</th><th>Why</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Your healthcare practice</td><td>They are treating you. Your measurements appear in your medical record.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Refresh Health</td><td>We run the software for them, on their instructions.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Amazon Web Services</td><td>They host our servers, in the United States, and make no use of what is on them.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Formspree</td><td>They deliver messages sent through the contact form on this website. They receive nothing from the app.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Anyone else</strong></td><td><strong>No one</strong>, except where the law compels us. Your health information is never sold, rented, or used for advertising.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>How long it is kept</h2>

    <p>Your measurements form part of your medical record, and your practice
      keeps that record for as long as the law requires them to.</p>

    <p>The sign-in and access records described above are kept for <strong>six
      years</strong>, which is the period United States health privacy rules
      require for records of this kind, and are then deleted.</p>

    <h2>Your rights, and how to use them</h2>

    <p>You can ask to:</p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>See</strong> the information held about you</li>
      <li><strong>Correct</strong> anything that is wrong</li>
      <li><strong>Delete</strong> information, where the law allows &mdash; a
        medical record usually cannot be deleted while a legal duty to keep it applies</li>
      <li><strong>Disconnect your phone</strong>, at any time, by asking your practice</li>
      <li><strong>Withdraw permission</strong> for the app to read Apple Health or
        Health Connect, in your phone&rsquo;s own settings</li>
      <li><strong>Complain</strong> &mdash; to us, to your practice, or to your
        country&rsquo;s data protection authority</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Ask your practice first, since they hold your record. You can also write to
      us at <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a> and we will
      help. We answer requests within thirty days.</p>

    <h2>State privacy rights</h2>

    <p>Several states give their residents further rights &mdash; among them
      California, Virginia, Colorado, Connecticut and Texas. These generally
      include the right to know what is held about you, to have it corrected or
      deleted, to obtain a copy, and not to be treated worse for asking.
      Washington&rsquo;s My Health My Data Act applies specifically to health
      information.</p>

    <p>To exercise any of these, write to
      <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>. We will not refuse
      you service, charge you differently, or give you a lesser standard of care
      for having asked.</p>

    <h2>Do Not Track</h2>

    <p>Browsers can send a &ldquo;Do Not Track&rdquo; signal. There is still no
      agreed standard for what a website should do with it, so we do not respond
      to it. This site does not track you in any case.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>

    <p>This app is given to a patient by their healthcare practice. Where the
      patient is a child, the practice arranges access with a parent or guardian,
      and the same protections in this policy apply.</p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>

    <p>If this policy changes in a way that affects you, we will update the date
      at the top and say what changed. The previous version stays available on
      request.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>

    <address class="legal__address">
      <strong>Refresh Health, Inc.</strong><br>
      4270 Falls Ridge Drive<br>
      Alpharetta, GA 30022<br>
      United States<br>
      <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>
    </address>

  </div>
</section>

</BaseLayout>
